<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability-second-assessor-gemini-4-argon> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Code-to-model traceability: 68/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "At commit 5659d5e (following commit 0154143), model constants are centralized, f2_for_shift() properly inverts wavefront_for_f2() without clipping, and Panel D dynamically formats pulse bounds (1.0-16.0 h) and posterior head-readout percentages (91.8% vs 23.5%) from simulation state. Deducts 32 points because the 1D RD equations and the pharynx-posterior phenotype threshold (x*_b = 0.5833, which includes 20-unit plotting padding and a 100-unit cartoon pharynx convention) do not map to published equations in Cervera et al. (2021)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 6.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity-second-assessor-gemini-4-argon> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Model fidelity to source: 50/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Explicitly documents in its header scope statement that the full texts of Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021) and Cervera et al. (2020) were not accessible and that the 1D reaction-diffusion solver (rd_antagonistic_1d and rd_linear_1d) and rusty-matter 2-node ODE port are qualitative analogues. At commit 5659d5e, f2 and f3 both drive distinct 1D boundary-value solvers, and the inverse threshold finder f2_for_shift() bisects on the unclipped wavefront x*(f2) = x*_b (recovering f2_b = 0.422 where x*(f2_b) = 0.5833). Held at 50 because the equations and constants are local constructions rather than verified transcriptions of the 2021/2020 papers, rd_antagonistic_1d's docstring (line 231) still claims to implement the paper's equations, and m3 (f3) is not coupled to any morphological boundary." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation-second-assessor-gemini-4-argon> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Morphometric validation: 54/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Fits a 1-parameter linear mapping f2(p) = 1 - a*p to Oviedo et al. (2010) octanol double-head frequencies across 4 axial crop positions (training RMSE = 4.19 percentage points) and evaluates it without refitting on held-out triple-innexin RNAi crops (test RMSE = 23.52 percentage points, r = 0.943), while verifying rusty-matter trace parity across all 5 scenarios (max |delta| = 0.0332) and computing Planform #1 vs #2 silhouette IoU (0.9478). Held at 54 because the 4-point empirical sample is tiny, the 23.5-point held-out error is large, and no morphometric dimensions of real regenerated double-head specimens are measured." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-measurement-anterior-body-area-fraction-on-s-mediterranea-silhouette-f2-1-f2-0-25>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-measurement-circuit-posterior-head-readout-memory-on-vs-memory-off-control>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-measurement-ml-centre-edge-ratio-f3-f3-1-0-vs-f3-0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-measurement-oviedo-2010-octanol-crop-gradient-training-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-measurement-oviedo-2010-triple-innexin-rnai-held-out-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-measurement-pharynx-boundary-criterion-x-b>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-measurement-planform-1-wild-type-vs-2-double-head-silhouette-iou>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-measurement-rusty-matter-trace-parity-max>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-measurement-symmetric-rd-wavefront-x-f2-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-overall-second-assessor-gemini-4-argon> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — MorphoEval overall 60.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Blinded second-assessor pass (gemini-4-argon) at commit 5659d5e (including the commit 0154143 fixes for f2_for_shift() and Panel D legend strings). Combines a local 1D reaction-diffusion analogue (AP m1/m2 + orthogonal ML m3), a deterministic Python port of the rusty-matter 2-node bioelectric circuit, a 1-parameter crop-position fit to Oviedo et al. (2010) octanol data tested on held-out innexin-RNAi data, and morphogen territory projection onto a segmented S. mediterranea photograph alongside two decoded Planform cartoons. Overall 60.7/100 (faithfulness 51.9, reproducibility 81.3; model-implementation 54.0/100, biological-validation 50.2/100, applicable-only overall 60.7/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5659d5e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 50, Morphological realism / specimen match 48, Parameter expressivity 62, Morphometric validation 54, Source and data traceability 84, Code-to-model traceability 68, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py at 5659d5e, image/gif, 1398777 B, 560×378 px, 46 frames, artifact_sha256 214238f0d75fdcfa702b96ce3fcb12fcafe48ed08e52c26bbcbfc1faf6bab427 (sha256 214238f0d75fdcfa702b96ce3fcb12fcafe48ed08e52c26bbcbfc1faf6bab427)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:hasScore 6.07e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity-second-assessor-gemini-4-argon> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Parameter expressivity: 62/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Sweeps f2 across [0.25, 1.0] (monotonically shifting the AP wavefront x*(f2) from 0.500 to 0.648 and anterior silhouette area from 0.483 to 0.639) and sweeps f3 across [0.30, 1.0] (reducing the ML centre/edge ratio lambda(f3) from 0.197 to 0.011), and compares 5 rusty-matter bioelectric scenarios across 3 crop positions. Deducts 38 points because f3 has no effect on the rendered 2D worm morphology and the phenotype output is a binary switch rather than a continuous morphogenetic deformation." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 6.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

