    dct:description "Segments a real Wikimedia Commons photograph of Schmidtea mediterranea (Stevenson & Beane 2010, SHA-256 verified) to measure the body-area fraction anterior to x*(f2) and renders decoded Planform #1 Wild Type and #2 Double Head cartoons. Held below 50 because the 1D signals are merely painted onto a static wild-type photograph whose outline never deforms into a double-headed worm, and the morphology readout switches categorically between two pre-drawn Planform cartoons at an assumed pharynx-posterior threshold x*_b = 0.5833." ;
