    dct:date "2026-10-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Blinded second-assessor pass (gemini-4-argon). Operationalises D'Arcy Thompson's freehand transformation grids (1917, Figs. 373-382) as a nested hierarchy of conformal and curvilinear coordinate families (similarity, affine, Moebius, coaxial circles via exact complex log-ratio and power-shear, and exact Bookstein 1989 thin-plate spline) fitted to 17 homologous landmarks across 791 Indo-Pacific fish species and tested on segmented museum/field specimen silhouettes. Overall 90.8/100 (faithfulness 89.9, reproducibility 93.1; model-implementation 90.0/100, biological-validation 89.8/100, applicable-only overall 90.8/100; uncalibrated rubric score, not a calibrated probability); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5659d5e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 96, Source and data traceability 97, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: thompson_scarus_pomacanthus.png: rendered output of thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py at 5659d5e, image/png, 739620 B, 2520×1540 px, artifact_sha256 d243f51e2b90b1a2201ec81265392b1cf95ea0f0e6e68074818cc5754b324e08 (sha256 d243f51e2b90b1a2201ec81265392b1cf95ea0f0e6e68074818cc5754b324e08)." ;
